<title>SWITZERLAND: WTO panel to study Brazil poultry complaint on EU.</title>
<headline>WTO panel to study Brazil poultry complaint on EU.</headline>
<dateline>GENEVA 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The World Trade Organisation set up a panel on Wednesday to look into complaints from Brazil that European Union regulations on imports of poultry products violate open trade rules, trade officials said.</p>
<p>Brazil complains that EU rules on imports of some poultry products run against agreements reached during the 1986-93 Uruguay Round of world trade negotiations.</p>
<p>Trade officials said Brazil told a meeting of the global trade body's Dispute Settlement Body (DSB) that the EU had failed to implement an earlier compensatory agreement with Brazil on poultry imports.</p>
<p>Brazil also told the body the EU was failing to implement a bilateral accord compensating Brazil for its oilseeds exports in the form of higher quotas for Brazilian poultry.</p>
<p>Brazilian companies say they are losing money in poultry exports to the EU because of the restrictions.</p>
<p>--- Reuters Geneva Newsroom 41-22-733 38 31</p>
